{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0A5F", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-finite-etale-over-proper}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:04642084f9e6ee541efdf1bed3e4ec03e60fd822b32ea6956946e5f79a84cf7c", "source_text": "First cohomology of proper schemes", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6b086d8d165d3150863f0f7c01fd1663f236314ca521357b893a71032f2ffce2", "unit_id": "tag:0A5F:title"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0A5F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R^1f_*\\underline{G}$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$G$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{pione-section-finite-etale-over-proper}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:eed7d656a71800daae765b88b3b4079cfc7baefaf6cf579b658cb4767ddef4cd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e877a0bbebc15a20abb1c2e2b9924c3b9221232ebca190282a5969b1d3ad6d59", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn Fundamental Groups, Section <REF_0001>\nwe have seen, in some sense, that taking\n<MATH_0001> commutes with base change if <MATH_0002>\nis a proper morphism and <MATH_0003> is a finite group (not necessarily\ncommutative). In this section\nwe deduce a useful consequence of these results.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ed9fdc179c6e442a62029d481937d0025bd0060597c33e9f40b40c2444419a67", "unit_id": "tag:0A5F:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0A5F", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$A$", "MATH_0004": "$X_0$", "MATH_0005": "$M$", "MATH_0006": "$H^1_\\etale(X, \\underline{M}) = H^1_\\etale(X_0, \\underline{M})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-proper-over-henselian-and-h1}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8782d70dd26bee22971d989b4a66e00a95f9c4be02d5224bd46e0573e7d5f476", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dd2c950e0562f409fbc9009acea8ae7ade87d558b8c4549b74d545b9ebba39cc", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a henselian local ring. Let <MATH_0002> be a proper scheme over <MATH_0003>\nwith closed fibre <MATH_0004>. Let <MATH_0005> be a finite abelian group.\nThen <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b00e92d8e1f3b2044b3fb410ff4e97d6485f56c31130fe521c18b7b49de334d5", "unit_id": "tag:0A5G:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0A5F", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$H^1_\\etale(X, \\underline{M})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\underline{M}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$V$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$V$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$M$", "MATH_0011": "$M$", "MATH_0012": "$X$", "MATH_0013": "$X_0$", "MATH_0014": "$X_0$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-lemma-torsors-h1}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-finite-locally-constant}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{pione-lemma-finite-etale-on-proper-over-henselian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ed241db5bc093880b44345d0bdebc73731ba7f2aee5acf6a94c0b1eb01e7265d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f91d3d1c2b4155335f8e97ef8e5e089c75db7cd17a99882f5f71db87b7620ef6", "source_text": "By Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <REF_0001>\nan element of <MATH_0001> corresponds to a\n<MATH_0002>-torsor <MATH_0003> on <MATH_0004>.\nSuch a torsor is clearly a finite locally constant sheaf.\nHence <MATH_0005> is representable by a scheme <MATH_0006> finite\n<ACCENT_0001>tale over <MATH_0007>, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nConversely, a scheme <MATH_0008> finite <ACCENT_0002>tale over <MATH_0009> with an <MATH_0010>-action\nwhich turns it into an <MATH_0011>-torsor over <MATH_0012> gives rise to a cohomology\nclass. The same translation between cohomology classes over <MATH_0013> and\ntorsors finite <ACCENT_0003>tale over <MATH_0014> holds. Thus the lemma\nis a consequence of the equivalence of categories of\nFundamental Groups, Lemma\n<REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:65fa0fb3bf47635a42c731a1c3456f1099afa9a72c686336628adefd82153ca8", "unit_id": "tag:0A5G:proof"}
